676
00:28:41,730 --> 00:28:44,340
And Team Deza and I support

677
00:28:44,340 --> 00:28:46,470
about 24 different workforce programs.

678
00:28:46,470 --> 00:28:49,263
And one of those happens to be automotive technology.

679
00:28:50,160 --> 00:28:53,040
And we have a partnership with Nuro

680
00:28:53,040 --> 00:28:55,640
and I'll tell you a little bit of how that happened.

681
00:28:56,880 --> 00:29:01,880
That was really a mind-blowing, earth-shattering partnership

682
00:29:02,730 --> 00:29:03,930
that we came with.

683
00:29:03,930 --> 00:29:07,830
We went to and talked with a company at the time was looking

684
00:29:07,830 --> 00:29:12,210
for four year degree technicians to work on their cars.

685
00:29:12,210 --> 00:29:14,460
And we found out what they really were after,

686
00:29:14,460 --> 00:29:17,160
and we found out what we already offered,

687
00:29:17,160 --> 00:29:20,730
and then we said, "Well, we already offer all those classes,

688
00:29:20,730 --> 00:29:22,860
why don't we repackage them

689
00:29:22,860 --> 00:29:24,180
and then we can have a certificate

690
00:29:24,180 --> 00:29:26,760
for autonomous driving vehicle technicians."

691
00:29:26,760 --> 00:29:29,160
And they said, "Yeah, that sounds good

692
00:29:29,160 --> 00:29:31,890
and let's go one step further.

693
00:29:31,890 --> 00:29:34,620
We're really interested in diversifying our workforce

694
00:29:34,620 --> 00:29:36,147
and that kind of thing."

695
00:29:36,147 --> 00:29:38,700
And I said, "Well, how about if we make the entry-level

696
00:29:38,700 --> 00:29:41,910
technician certificate non-credit,

697
00:29:41,910 --> 00:29:43,470
would you go there?"

698
00:29:43,470 --> 00:29:45,510
And they said, "Yeah, we'll go there."

699
00:29:45,510 --> 00:29:48,903
And that was like, gimme some oxygen.

700
00:29:49,830 --> 00:29:51,690
You know, how does that work?

701
00:29:51,690 --> 00:29:54,630
So, it's just astonishing the partnership

702
00:29:54,630 --> 00:29:56,130
that we developed there.

703
00:29:56,130 --> 00:29:57,930
From that, other companies have talked

704
00:29:57,930 --> 00:29:59,490
to us about spinning off

705
00:29:59,490 --> 00:30:02,400
from that autonomous driving vehicle certificate

706
00:30:02,400 --> 00:30:03,550
and doing other things.

707
00:30:05,700 --> 00:30:08,250
One of the things that came up in the process

708
00:30:08,250 --> 00:30:09,840
is that different companies would come

709
00:30:09,840 --> 00:30:11,240
and talk to us about...

710
00:30:12,150 --> 00:30:13,389
This ain't working.

711
00:30:13,389 --> 00:30:14,222
I don't think it's working.

712
00:30:14,222 --> 00:30:16,830
So, I don't know if we...

713
00:30:16,830 --> 00:30:18,293
I'll use my teacher voice.

714
00:30:18,293 --> 00:30:20,190
(audience tittering)

715
00:30:20,190 --> 00:30:21,757
So, they would come and say, you know,

716
00:30:21,757 --> 00:30:24,920
"We have this thing but we don't have..."

717
00:30:24,920 --> 00:30:25,753
Is that better?

718
00:30:25,753 --> 00:30:27,270
Okay, there you go.

719
00:30:27,270 --> 00:30:32,160
So, "But we need to add this to what you're training,"

720
00:30:32,160 --> 00:30:36,330
and the community college system is notoriously slow

721
00:30:36,330 --> 00:30:37,530
for developing curriculum.

722
00:30:37,530 --> 00:30:38,730
Well, we can develop the curriculum,

723
00:30:38,730 --> 00:30:40,920
but by the time it gets through the process

724
00:30:40,920 --> 00:30:42,780
and gets through the college process, it's a year

725
00:30:42,780 --> 00:30:45,690
to two years before we can offer the courses.

726
00:30:45,690 --> 00:30:48,540
So, we did a lot of streamlining in the non-credit world

727
00:30:48,540 --> 00:30:49,830
where we can offer that quickly

728
00:30:49,830 --> 00:30:51,630
and we're working at that.

729
00:30:51,630 --> 00:30:56,490
But we also stood up a contract education not for credit,

730
00:30:56,490 --> 00:30:58,620
where we can take our basic program,

731
00:30:58,620 --> 00:31:00,000
which is a two year certificate

732
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:02,460
or a degree in autonomous driving

733
00:31:02,460 --> 00:31:06,930
and add any company's proprietary training

734
00:31:06,930 --> 00:31:08,430
in the contract ed section.

735
00:31:08,430 --> 00:31:11,580
We can use our instructors, their instructors,

736
00:31:11,580 --> 00:31:12,870
we can teach it at our facility,

737
00:31:12,870 --> 00:31:15,390
we can teach it at their facility, it doesn't matter.

738
00:31:15,390 --> 00:31:17,580
So, all of those kind of conversations

739
00:31:17,580 --> 00:31:20,100
came from the Nuro partnership that we did.

740
00:31:20,100 --> 00:31:22,590
And it's really astonishing

741
00:31:22,590 --> 00:31:26,280
and the opportunities that it brings to our students

742
00:31:26,280 --> 00:31:29,080
and to a lot of our favorite students

743
00:31:30,060 --> 00:31:32,370
in automotive test students, of course,

744
00:31:32,370 --> 00:31:37,290
you know that is a option that didn't exist before.

745
00:31:37,290 --> 00:31:39,810
So, it was really astonishing and I applaud Nuro

746
00:31:39,810 --> 00:31:41,280
for leaning forward to that.

747
00:31:41,280 --> 00:31:44,130
But to go from a four year engineering degree requirement

748
00:31:44,970 --> 00:31:47,850
all the way to a non-credit entry level certificate

749
00:31:47,850 --> 00:31:48,810
opened up doors

750
00:31:48,810 --> 00:31:51,990
to our most marginalized students and opportunity.

751
00:31:51,990 --> 00:31:54,310
We have so many brilliant young people

752
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:58,680
that aren't gonna ever be able to go to Berkeley

753
00:31:58,680 --> 00:32:02,250
or San Jose State or anything else because of life, right?

754
00:32:02,250 --> 00:32:03,450
But they're brilliant people

755
00:32:03,450 --> 00:32:06,345
and if we give them the opportunity, they will succeed

756
00:32:06,345 --> 00:32:07,710
and be great.

757
00:32:07,710 --> 00:32:10,530
And Nuro has really helped with that program.

758
00:32:10,530 --> 00:32:12,150
So,

759
00:32:12,150 --> 00:32:15,270
so far we've got nine students

760
00:32:15,270 --> 00:32:16,710
that have completed the certificate

761
00:32:16,710 --> 00:32:21,710
and another six, no, another eight that are in process now.

762
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:24,150
So, we're moving forward,

763
00:32:24,150 --> 00:32:26,460
and those students are coming out of the pipeline now,

764
00:32:26,460 --> 00:32:28,977
and so hopefully for Rivian and Nuro

765
00:32:28,977 --> 00:32:32,880
and others, we'll be able to help them fulfill that need.

766
00:32:32,880 --> 00:32:35,610
Now, they translate all the way across

767
00:32:35,610 --> 00:32:39,420
the whole spectrum, which is eVTOL, right?

768
00:32:39,420 --> 00:32:42,030
That's the vertical landing and takeoff vehicles,

769
00:32:42,030 --> 00:32:44,430
that's cars, that's trucks.

770
00:32:44,430 --> 00:32:46,890
They go across the whole spectrum

771
00:32:46,890 --> 00:32:49,290
and then they can go into Berkeley

772
00:32:49,290 --> 00:32:51,750
and work at the Richmond thing

773
00:32:51,750 --> 00:32:53,430
and get into battery production.

774
00:32:53,430 --> 00:32:57,180
There's so much is gonna be required in the near future

775
00:32:57,180 --> 00:32:59,940
and we're on the way and have a program established

776
00:32:59,940 --> 00:33:02,400
and we just gotta grow it.

777
00:33:02,400 --> 00:33:03,810
The other piece that's really important

778
00:33:03,810 --> 00:33:05,730
about the community college system and the training

779
00:33:05,730 --> 00:33:07,230
that we can provide

780
00:33:07,230 --> 00:33:11,430
is the partnership that we have as a community of colleges.

781
00:33:11,430 --> 00:33:13,080
You know, like Silicon Valley colleges

782
00:33:13,080 --> 00:33:14,460
are all working together now

783
00:33:14,460 --> 00:33:19,080
in the industrial automation area to develop

784
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:21,300
programs where you could take a little bit

785
00:33:21,300 --> 00:33:23,040
from this college, a little bit from that college

786
00:33:23,040 --> 00:33:25,790
and put it together and make a certificate or a degree.

787
00:33:27,540 --> 00:33:30,840
And that's like, that's new and exciting, (laughs)

788
00:33:30,840 --> 00:33:32,370
basically earth-shattering.

789
00:33:32,370 --> 00:33:34,020
We're all in the same room and we talk

790
00:33:34,020 --> 00:33:35,340
to each other and we're nice to each other.

791
00:33:35,340 --> 00:33:37,022
So, it's pretty good.

792
00:33:37,022 --> 00:33:37,855
(audience member laughing)

